-- Sovietski: the Tsar "Big Ivan" Superheavy Machine and the full conversion cyborg birds of prey (falcon or hawk, and steppe eagle), WB36 cyborg bodies with no WB17 counterpart, held as new rows (printed 145-150).
-- 3 vehicle rows, with 21 locations and 8 weapon entries.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~397-sovietski-cyborgs-d.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/vessel-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every value
-- is printable ASCII, every row cites its book, and a Main Body location
-- agrees with its vehicle's mdc_main_body.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
  ('sovietski-tsar-superheavy-machine', 'Sovietski Tsar Superheavy Machine', 'rifts', 'borg', 'One human volunteer (full conversion).', 'None.', 'Running: 50 mph (80 km) maximum. Leaping: 10 feet (3 m) high or 20 feet (6.1 m) lengthwise; top-heavy, so a running start adds nothing.', 'None; too heavy and bulky to fly.', 'Cannot swim and sinks. With an oxygen storage cell it walks the bottom of rivers and waterways at 8 mph (13 km). Maximum depth 1,200 feet (366 m).', 'Height 15 feet (4.6 m); width 6 feet (1.8 m); length 5 feet (1.5 m).', '7 tons.', 740, 1, NULL, 5500000, 'Sovietski cost 5.5 million credits; 8-9 million credits on the Black Market, rare. The Sovietski figure is stored.', 'The Tsar, called Big Ivan by the infantry and by other cyborgs (loyal communists tend to prefer the nickname to the royal name), is a Superheavy Machine said to be built on a pre-Rifts walking-tank chassis recovered from the Kaliningrad Research Complex. It is a huge bipedal frame of Mega-Damage composite alloy with extra plating bolted over the body, arms, legs and the armored ammunition drum on its back. It is slow, big and an easy target, and its makers have found that the less human a body looks, the more its occupant drifts from humanity and toward cruelty in battle. Former Tankers, drivers and gunners above all, cope best: they treat the giant body as a tank they ride in, and keep a Light Machine body as their real self for leave, formal duty and retirement, so many badly wounded Tankers choose to become a Big Ivan. Its signature weapon is the Empress Cannon, a handheld rail cannon on a back-mounted connector arm that swings it behind the left shoulder when not in use; a belt feeds it from the back drum. If the belt is lost each round must be hand-loaded from the drum, which takes three actions, and if the connector arm is lost the cyborg must carry the gun or abandon it (most hide or wreck it first). The opening text also mentions chest mini-missiles and a single right-forearm ion blaster; the weapon list prints no mini-missiles and puts an ion blaster in each forearm. Robot P.S. 45 and Robot P.P. 20: 1D6 M.D. restrained punch, 3D6 M.D. full punch, 1D6x10 M.D. power punch (two attacks), 5D8 M.D. kick; it cannot leap kick. A full speed ram or body block does 3D6+3 M.D., uses two attacks, and has a 01-75% chance to knock down anyone under two tons, who loses two attacks and initiative. Bonuses: one extra attack per melee, strike and parry +2, pull punch +1. Penalties: -60% to Prowl, and with tactile sensitivity of 35%, -40% to Forgery, Picking Locks, Picking Pockets, surgery, Whittling/Sculpting, Art and any fine-fingered skill. Its stat block prints no power system; its ion blasters run off a nuclear supply. Bionic features: every standard Sovietski Heavy Machine feature, plus a super-telescopic eye, a multi-system eye socket, stabilizing anchors, a combat computer and the ranged combat enhancement program. Starting weapons and features: one large leg compartment or leg weapon per leg, a face (usually a youthful version of its own, hidden by the helmet in combat), three more eye or head features, handheld weapons sized for a Heavy or Superheavy Machine only, and three Micro-Repair Robots plus two Cyber-Nano-Robot Repair Systems. Its armor is bolted on as built, so it takes no add-on plating; only the helmet adds 80 M.D.C. Chop-shops, Warlord camps, Mindwerks and some mercenaries will fit its weapon systems to Shocktroopers or Superheavy Machines for a price.', 'Rifts World Book 36: Sovietski p.145-147'),
  ('sovietski-cyborg-falcon-or-hawk', 'Sovietski Cyborg Bird of Prey (Falcon or Hawk)', 'rifts', 'borg', 'One falcon or hawk (Enhanced Cybernetic Animal, full conversion Ultra-Light Machine).', 'None.', 'Running: 5 mph (8 km); prefers to fly. Leaping: as normal for the species, typically a foot (0.3 m) without taking off.', 'Sustained flight 50 mph (80 km) without fatigue; dives at 200 mph (320 km) with a small thruster behind each upper leg, which also gives bursts of 200 mph (320 km) for 1D4+3 melee rounds (60-105 seconds) to attack or flee.', 'None.', 'Falcon: 18 inches (46 cm) tall, wingspan 2 feet, 6 inches to 3 feet, 8 inches (0.8 to 1.1 m). Hawk: one foot (0.3 m) tall, wingspan 3-4 feet (0.9 to 1.2 m).', '10 pounds (4.5 kg).', 20, 1, NULL, 390000, 'Sovietski cost 390,000 credits for a full conversion; 70,000 credits for a partial cyborg, which keeps the bird''s ordinary flight and has no M.D.C. Never sold on the Black Market. The full conversion figure is stored.', 'A falcon or hawk rebuilt as a flying scout under the Sovietski''s Enhanced Animal Cyborg Program, which also makes cyborg dogs, bears and the bionic horses of Warlords of Russia. Every enhanced animal carries a Neural Aggression Modulator Control (NAMC) implant, matched to one in its assigned handler, that makes the beast treat that person as its own kind and leader, keeps it calm under fire and lets it obey even wounded or afraid; one handler leads up to four such animals, and each animal''s weapon power systems can be pulled out and swapped as needed. The program is experimental, Top Secret and the Sovietski''s alone. Bird handlers are trained falconers, and the raptors serve snipers, point men, forward scouts, commanders, Spetsnaz and now and then commandos as a living drone: camera eyes send all they see back to base, and they also carry messages, light tools, supplies, and sometimes explosives to drop. The full conversion has bionic wings, spine and legs, light M.D.C. ceramic and plastic armor on the head and chest, and Vibro-Blade talons; it is about 10% bigger than a natural bird and usually keeps its own feathers, so it passes for a wild bird unless seen close up. It is not built for a stand-up fight. Robot P.S. 13 and Robot P.P. 18: 1D6 S.D.C. on a restrained bite or talon strike, 2D6+3 S.D.C. on a full talon strike, 4D6+4 S.D.C. diving talon strike (two attacks); the Vibro-Talons deal M.D. Four attacks per melee, NAMC bonus included. Bonuses (NAMC included): +15% to Climbing, initiative +2, strike and dodge +3. Natural abilities: Prowl 80% (lost while the thrusters fire), nightvision to 400 feet (122 m), track by smell 46%, track by sight 80%. Power: an internal battery runs every system for 96 hours, recharged by small fold-out solar panels on the back, with an E-Clip port good for 48 more hours per clip; removing it shuts the weapons down while leaving the bird some freedom. Bionic features: a Cyber-Camera Eye with telescopic sight (60 mile/96 km transmission range) and an Optic Nerve Video Implant (both Rifts Ultimate Edition p.50), booster jets, the fold-out solar recharger, a concealed E-Clip port, two Multi-System Eye Sockets, and a built-in radio transmitter and receiver (5 miles/8 km).', 'Rifts World Book 36: Sovietski p.148-150'),
  ('sovietski-cyborg-steppe-eagle', 'Sovietski Cyborg Bird of Prey (Steppe Eagle)', 'rifts', 'borg', 'One steppe eagle (Enhanced Cybernetic Animal, full conversion Ultra-Light Machine).', 'None.', 'Running: 5 mph (8 km); prefers to fly. Leaping: as normal for the species, typically a foot (0.3 m) without taking off.', 'Sustained flight 80 mph (128 km); dives at 300 mph (480 km) with a small thruster behind each upper leg, which also gives bursts of 300 mph (480 km) for 1D4+8 melee rounds (2-3 minutes) to attack or flee.', 'None.', '2-3 feet (0.6 to 0.9 m) tall; wingspan 7 feet (2.1 m).', '35 pounds (16 kg).', 40, 1, NULL, 390000, 'Sovietski cost 390,000 credits for a full conversion; 70,000 credits for a partial cyborg, which keeps the bird''s ordinary flight and has no M.D.C. Never sold on the Black Market. The book prices birds of prey as one; the full conversion figure is stored.', 'The eagle version of the Sovietski''s cyborg bird of prey, almost always a steppe eagle from the steppes, deserts and semi-deserts that run from Eastern Europe across Russia and Mongolia to Asia and India. It shares the falcon and hawk''s stat block, NAMC implant, role and bionic features, with heavier armor, faster flight and harder-hitting talons. Under the Enhanced Animal Cyborg Program a NAMC implant matched to one in its handler makes the bird treat that person as its own kind and leader, keeps it calm under fire and lets it obey even wounded or afraid; one handler leads up to four such animals, and the weapon power systems can be pulled out and swapped as needed. The program is experimental, Top Secret and the Sovietski''s alone. It serves snipers, point men, scouts, commanders, Spetsnaz and now and then commandos as a living drone, sending all it sees back to base, and also carries messages, light tools, supplies and sometimes explosives. The full conversion has bionic wings, spine and legs, light M.D.C. ceramic and plastic armor on the head and chest, and Vibro-Blade talons; about 10% larger than a natural bird and usually keeping its feathers, it passes for a wild one unless seen up close. It is not built for a stand-up fight. Robot P.S. 13 and Robot P.P. 18: 1D6 S.D.C. on a restrained bite or talon strike, 2D6+3 S.D.C. on a full talon strike, 4D6+4 S.D.C. diving talon strike (two attacks); the Vibro-Talons deal M.D. Four attacks per melee, NAMC bonus included. Bonuses (NAMC included): +15% to Climbing, initiative +2, strike and dodge +3. Natural abilities: Prowl 80% (lost while the thrusters fire), nightvision to 400 feet (122 m), track by smell 46%, track by sight 80%. Power: an internal battery runs every system for 96 hours, recharged by small fold-out solar panels on the back, with an E-Clip port good for 48 more hours per clip; removing it shuts the weapons down while leaving the bird some freedom. Bionic features: a Cyber-Camera Eye with telescopic sight (60 mile/96 km transmission range) and an Optic Nerve Video Implant (both Rifts Ultimate Edition p.50), booster jets, the fold-out solar recharger, a concealed E-Clip port, two Multi-System Eye Sockets, and a built-in radio transmitter and receiver (5 miles/8 km).', 'Rifts World Book 36: Sovietski p.148-150');

